    }
  ],
  "source_findings": [
    {
      "fact": "The test replaces /dir2 with a Mockito spy via root.replaceChild in the JUnit thread before issuing hdfs.rename. The setup invocation is hdfs-client, so it cannot substitute for the selected named NameNode target.",
      "kind": "direct_test_setup_target",
      "location": "TestRenameWithSnapshots.java:1351-1360"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The NameNode rename path constructs RenameOperation and may call replaceChild4ReferenceWithName, which calls replaceChild. The relevant interval manipulates in-memory namespace references and quota structures; no file write or nested RPC precedes that check within this interval.",
      "kind": "in_memory_namenode_target",
      "location": "FSDirRenameOp.java:203-233, 640-690; INodeDirectory.java:351-399"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The observed RpcCall.run door is immediately before Server.call(...). An injected IOException enters the surrounding Throwable catch and becomes an RPC error response; the rename handler and its replaceChild target are not entered for that request.",
      "kind": "rpc_door_aborts_handler",
      "location": "Server.java:1235-1254"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The deprecated rename used by hdfs.rename reaches FSDirRenameOp.renameToInt first. FSNamesystem.logSync is conditional on successful rename and occurs after the rename operation. FSDirRenameOp.logRename likewise follows unprotectedRenameTo. Neither is a pre-target file I/O door.",
      "kind": "edit_log_io_after_target",
      "location": "FSNamesystem.java:3300-3330; FSDirRenameOp.java:203-233, 505-525"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The method issues mkdir, createFile, snapshot, and rename in sequence without a catch/retry around these calls. The selected rename is expected to return false, not throw an injected IOException. Earlier RPC errors generally abort this JUnit before the NameNode target.",
